      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2020-october/q3",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:80mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9fm0-01-2020-october/q03-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1: polar curves about the pole O with the initial line drawn to the right; C2 is a large cardioid-shaped curve below the initial line with its cusp at O, and C1 is a small cardioid above O; the region R inside C1 and outside C2 is shaded.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a sketch of two curves <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\"></span> with polar equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C_1:\\ r=(1+\\sin\\theta)\\qquad 0\\leqslant\\theta&lt;2\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C_2:\\ r=3(1-\\sin\\theta)\\qquad 0\\leqslant\\theta&lt;2\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> lies inside <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span> and outside <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\"></span> and is shown shaded in Figure 1.</p><p>Show that the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"p\\sqrt3-q\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> are integers to be determined. <span class=\"marks\">(9)</span></p>",
