      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2020-october/q7",
      "question": "<p>A sample of bacteria in a sealed container is being studied.</p><p>The number of bacteria, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, in thousands, is modelled by the differential equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+t)\\frac{\\mathrm dP}{\\mathrm dt}+P=t^{\\frac12}(1+t)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> is the time in hours after the start of the study.</p><p>Initially, there are exactly 5000 bacteria in the container.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Determine, according to the model, the number of bacteria in the container 8 hours after the start of the study. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li><li>Find, according to the model, the rate of change of the number of bacteria in the container 4 hours after the start of the study. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>State a limitation of the model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
